# 🛠️ Sub-Phase 1: Windows Server Core Roles & Feature Configuration

This module documents the initial configuration of the Windows Server environment, specifically focusing on the deployment of Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS) and necessary migration features.

## 📋 Server Role Deployment Walkthrough

| Step | Action | Technical Description | Screenshot Reference |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **01** | **Initialize Server Manager** | Launch the Server Manager Dashboard and navigate to the **Manage** menu to initiate the 'Add Roles and Features' wizard. | ![Step 1](./images/image%201.png) |
| **02** | **Deployment Type** | Selecting **Role-based or feature-based installation** to configure the local server instance with specific service capabilities. | ![Step 2](./images/image%202.png) |
| **03** | **Active Directory Setup** | Enabling **Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)**. Note: The Web Server (IIS) role is deselected to minimize the server's attack surface and focus on Identity Management. | ![Step 3](./images/image%203.png) |
| **04** | **Feature Selection** | Provisioning **Wireless LAN Services** and **Windows Server Migration Tools** to support infrastructure mobility and data transfer. | ![Step 4](./images/image%204.png) |
| **05** | **Dashboard Overview** | Final verification of the Server Manager Dashboard post-selection, showing the pending installation status and role overview. | ![Step 5](./images/image%205.png) |

---

## 💡 System Administrator's Note
When configuring a Domain Controller, it is best practice to only install necessary roles. By deselecting **Web Server (IIS)** in Step 3, we reduce unnecessary background services, which improves both system performance and security.

